stdexec 6d7ad689: count bwos::lifo_queue's blocks linearly in 64 bits.

last_block_, start_block_ and the counters derived from them pack a round
above bit 32 and an index below it, but are declared std::size_t. Where
std::size_t has 32 bits (wasm32, i386) the shifts by 32 are undefined: the
queue refuses pushes as if full or never returns, and static_thread_pool
runs few or none of the tasks given to it. This replaces the packing with
a linear std::uint64_t block counter, counter = round * num_blocks + index:
the index is counter & mask_, the round is counter >> log2(num_blocks), and
the next or previous block is counter + 1 or counter - 1, so
increase_block_counter and decrease_block_counter are gone. The same
change is offered to stdexec upstream against main; this copy is
rebased on 6d7ad689, where three hunks differed only in comments.
Applied by cmake/StdFeatures.cmake to builds with 32-bit pointers only.

--- a/include/exec/detail/bwos_lifo_queue.hpp
